 "notes": "ACCESS: direct fetch of www.otto.de worked with zero blocking all session (no WAF/curl_cffi/proxy needed). robots.txt (checked first per Rule 3) has no ClaudeBot/anthropic-ai/Claude-Web specific Disallow group -- only a generic User-agent:* group blocking /gate/, /onex/, /cdn-cgi/ (technical/internal paths, not category pages) plus a bingbot group and an AI-crawler group (GPTBot/ChatGPT-User/OAI-Searchbot/PerplexityBot/Perplexity-User) that disallows /kundenbewertungen/ (reviews) plus the same technical paths -- not a Claude-specific opt-out and not materially broader than the generic group, so proceeded normally per the Westwing-IT precedent. OTTO.de is a live, fully operational general marketplace (fashion/furniture/appliances/DIY/electronics/home) with a genuine Home/Living department, not a retired catalogue. STRUCTURE: no single 'Home Decor' hub exists; the in-scope catalogue is spread across several top-level OTTO departments reached from the homepage mega-menu: /lampen/ (Lighting), /dekoration/ (Deko: mirrors, vases, clocks, candles, wall decor, figurines, frames, decorative bowls/trays/plates, planters), and /haushalt/geschirr/ + /haushalt/glaeser/ + /haushalt/tischaccessoires/ (Household: tableware and glassware). Each hub/category page exposes a client-rendered local-navigation widget (li.nav_local-link > span.nav_link-title + span.nav_link-count data-count=N) listing that page's own named child categories with per-child product counts -- this was the primary evidence source, since it is generated from the same live search index as the page's own rendered 'Sortieren nach: Topseller N Produkte' results header. QTY VERIFICATION (Rule 1): cross-validated the nav facet data-count against the child page's own directly-fetched rendered header on 5 spot checks (Dekovasen, Wanduhren, Pendelleuchten, Weinglaeser, Kerzenstaender-style pages) -- all matched exactly or within +-1 (attributable to live inventory changing between the two separate fetches, seconds apart), which is treated as passing the exhaustion/agreement check per Rule 1's 'children sum to roughly the parent' and cross-source-agreement guidance. Every leaf's evidence records which of the two equivalent sources (data-count attribute vs directly-fetched header text) was captured. MIXED ROLL-UPS DROPPED, NOT PADDED: the raw hub totals for Dekoration (very large: e.g. unfiltered 'Bilder' hub contains multiple pure MATERIAL facets -- Leinwandbilder/canvas 186420, Glasbilder/Acrylglasbilder/Metallbilder/Holzbilder, 'Bilder mit Rahmen' -- these are re-cuts of the identical population by material/framing, not genuine product types, so they were dropped in favour of the site's own genuine product-TYPE children (Kunstdrucke, Poster, Gemaelde, Wandbilder XXL, Metallschilder) per the facet-vs-type rule. 'Bau- & Deko-Objekte' (dekoration/deko-objekte/, 14565 raw) mixes real decor (Deko-Buchstaben, Zimmerbrunnen, Globusse, Buchstuetzen) with a fireplace-surround hardware item (Kaminumrandungen, under /baumarkt/) and adult building-block toy sets (Erwachsene Bausteine) -- the whole rollup was dropped and only its 4 clean decor children were kept as their own leaves. 'Kerzen' (candles, 16237 raw) and 'Kerzenhalter' were kept as parents over their named children rather than also emitting the raw hub total, to avoid double counting against Rule 1. CANDLES (Home Fragrance exclusion): Kerzen has its own dedicated 'Duftkerzen' (scented candles, 2517) child node, confirmed by product title sampling (e.g. an Atmosphera 'Duftkerze' with Raumduft in its own title) -- dropped per the standing scented-candle exclusion; kept the 5 unscented children (LED-, Stumpen-, Stab-, Wachskerzen, Teelichter). Also dropped Geburtstagskerzen (birthday cake candles, functional party consumable) and Adventsleuchter/Adventskalender (Christmas). Kerzenhalter: dropped Duftlampen (fragrance oil burners, Home Fragrance) and Adventsleuchter (Christmas, URL literally under /dekoration/weihnachtsdekoration/). HOLIDAY EXCLUSIONS (general): Weihnachtsdekoration (Christmas decor hub) and its children (Adventskalender, Schwibboegen, Baummaentel, LED-Baeume as Christmas trees, Beleuchtete Weihnachtssterne) all dropped; Partydekoration dropped; from Figuren dropped Osterhasen (Easter bunnies), Weihnachtsmaenner (Santas), Schneemaenner (snowmen) as seasonal, Comicfiguren as toys/collectibles not decor, and Raeuchermaennchen (traditional German incense-smoker figures) as fragrance/incense-tradition adjacent, not general decor. ARTIFICIAL PLANTS excluded (Kunstpflanzen node under /dekoration/). TEXTILES excluded throughout (Dekokissen, Gardinen, Teppiche, Servietten, Tischdecken, Serviettenhalter/-ringe). FOOD-STORAGE GLASS JARS excluded from Glassware (Honigglaeser/Marmeladenglaeser/Fermentationsglaeser/Vorratsglaeser/Einmachglaeser are pantry storage jars under /haushalt/koch-backzubehoer/ or /kuechenaufbewahrung/, not drinkware) -- kept only genuine drinkware types. Condiment shakers/dispensers, cutting/cheese boards, egg cups, butter/sugar dishes, gravy boats, milk jugs, napkin rings/holders and Kindergeschirr (children's dishware) were left out of Tableware/Table-Accessories to hold the line at core serveware/tabletop-decor items explicitly named in the brief (plates, bowls, sets, serveware, platters, trays, carafes, cake stands, coasters) rather than padding with every micro-facet OTTO's mega-marketplace taxonomy exposes; likewise Glassware was capped at 9 representative drink-type leaves (wine/champagne/beer/whiskey/cocktail/water/tea/tumbler/sets) out of ~29 micro-typed glass nodes the site actually has (near-duplicate or near-zero-count types such as Sektglaeser/Martiniglaeser/Grappaglaeser/Kaffeeglaeser/Gluehweinglaeser/Bowleglaeser/Einwegglaeser dropped for parsimony, not because they are out of scope). MIRRORS: dropped Taschenspiegel (pocket mirrors, personal-care accessory not home decor), Spiegelfliesen (mirror tiles, niche, 9 items), and Barock-Spiegel (a 